				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "98e5de3f-fd00-45d5-81f6-e47b9db4abac")
	)
	(text "I made no attempt to prevent backpowering from\nthe USB devices onto the 5V+ rail but protection\ncould be accomplished through ideal diodes. \nRaspberry pi does not protect from backpowering."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 247.142 29.972 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "a047d010-e4b3-456f-8fd8-0ef05dd05f7a")
	)
	(text "I would like this to be two directinonal so that board could\nbe powered from the USB C.\nI would need to do some work to get that working in both\ndirection so that it can be powered and give power from\nthis port"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 192.786 110.49 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "da91c0a7-7b90-4898-a608-2dc02294ff63")
	)
	(text "ISET is for the GANG power overcurrent detection\nto set the combined current for the USB ports.\nThe equation is:\nIset(Amps) = 60K / Rset\nwhere Rset is the value of the external resistor.\nI chose 51K to limit to 1.17Amps total power\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 247.65 49.022 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "f75a2836-da77-45f8-8209-df515cb7a04a")
	)
